  "segments": [
   {
    "id": "t1",
    "start": 0.0,
    "end": 1.96,
    "text": "Is fruit making Americans fat?"
   },
   {
    "id": "t2",
    "start": 1.96,
    "end": 2.8,
    "text": "Yes."
   },
   {
    "id": "t3",
    "start": 2.8,
    "end": 4.4,
    "text": "No, no it's not."
   },
   {
    "id": "t4",
    "start": 4.4,
    "end": 6.16,
    "text": "Fructose, for one thing, you know,"
   },
   {
    "id": "t5",
    "start": 6.16,
    "end": 7.04,
    "text": "all fruit breaks down to sugar,"
   },
   {
    "id": "t6",
    "start": 7.04,
    "end": 8.84,
    "text": "but then it also breaks down to fructose,"
   },
   {
    "id": "t7",
    "start": 8.84,
    "end": 11.24,
    "text": "which creates a lot of visceral fat."
   },
   {
    "id": "t8",
    "start": 11.24,
    "end": 12.68,
    "text": "So fructose is really hard on the liver,"
   },
   {
    "id": "t9",
    "start": 12.68,
    "end": 14.0,
    "text": "the liver has a hard time processing it,"
   },
   {
    "id": "t10",
    "start": 14.0,
    "end": 16.44,
    "text": "but it also creates a lot of internal fat."
   },
   {
    "id": "t11",
    "start": 16.44,
    "end": 18.44,
    "text": "So you see a lot of the vegans or a lot of the girls"
   },
   {
    "id": "t12",
    "start": 18.44,
    "end": 20.08,
    "text": "that are like these fraught fruity girls"
   },
   {
    "id": "t13",
    "start": 20.08,
    "end": 21.28,
    "text": "and they're like walking around"
   },
   {
    "id": "t14",
    "start": 21.28,
    "end": 22.88,
    "text": "and they seem like they're really thin,"
   },
   {
    "id": "t15",
    "start": 22.88,
    "end": 24.88,
    "text": "but what they don't know is they're loaded with fat inside."
   },
   {
    "id": "t16",
    "start": 24.88,
    "end": 26.56,
    "text": "All their organs are suffocating in fat."
   },
   {
    "id": "t17",
    "start": 26.56,
    "end": 27.4,
    "text": "What?"
   },
   {
    "id": "t18",
    "start": 27.4,
    "end": 28.84,
    "text": "First of all, why are we showing B-roll"
   },
   {
    "id": "t19",
    "start": 28.84,
    "end": 30.68,
    "text": "of that joyful woman making her food"
   },
   {
    "id": "t20",
    "start": 30.68,
    "end": 32.96,
    "text": "while these two talk about pseudoscience on a podcast."
   },
   {
    "id": "t21",
    "start": 32.96,
    "end": 34.8,
    "text": "Fruit is not making Americans fat."
   },
   {
    "id": "t22",
    "start": 34.8,
    "end": 38.2,
    "text": "88% of Americans don't even meet fruit intake guidelines."
   },
   {
    "id": "t23",
    "start": 38.2,
    "end": 40.72,
    "text": "And the state with the lowest fruit intake is West Virginia,"
   },
   {
    "id": "t24",
    "start": 40.72,
    "end": 42.68,
    "text": "which is the state with the highest obesity rates"
   },
   {
    "id": "t25",
    "start": 42.68,
    "end": 43.52,
    "text": "in the country."
   },
   {
    "id": "t26",
    "start": 43.52,
    "end": 45.8,
    "text": "And actual scientific research consistently shows"
   },
   {
    "id": "t27",
    "start": 45.8,
    "end": 48.36,
    "text": "that higher fruit intakes are linked to lower risk"
   },
   {
    "id": "t28",
    "start": 48.36,
    "end": 51.0,
    "text": "of obesity, heart disease, and fatty liver disease."
   },
   {
    "id": "t29",
    "start": 51.0,
    "end": 52.72,
    "text": "This is a perfect example of pseudoscience"
   },
   {
    "id": "t30",
    "start": 52.72,
    "end": 54.72,
    "text": "when something is presented as scientific"
   },
   {
    "id": "t31",
    "start": 54.72,
    "end": 55.96,
    "text": "with science-y sounding words,"
   },
   {
    "id": "t32",
    "start": 55.96,
    "end": 57.8,
    "text": "but it lacks any actual science."
   },
   {
    "id": "t33",
    "start": 57.8,
    "end": 61.2,
    "text": "They'll start with a true or somewhat true mechanism, like here, where she talks about"
   },
   {
    "id": "t34",
    "start": 61.2,
    "end": 64.92,
    "text": "how fructose is processed in the liver, and that can lead to an accumulation of visceral"
   },
   {
    "id": "t35",
    "start": 64.92,
    "end": 65.92,
    "text": "fat."
   },
   {
    "id": "t36",
    "start": 65.92,
    "end": 68.72,
    "text": "But then they won't provide any context for that, like the dose necessary to elicit"
   },
   {
    "id": "t37",
    "start": 68.72,
    "end": 72.54,
    "text": "that response, or the difference between fructose that's found in fruit with all of the other"
   },
   {
    "id": "t38",
    "start": 72.54,
    "end": 76.6,
    "text": "things found in fruit and the fructose frowned in soda, the role of fiber in fruit, or the"
   },
   {
    "id": "t39",
    "start": 76.6,
    "end": 79.7,
    "text": "totality of evidence going against what she's saying."
   },
   {
    "id": "t40",
    "start": 79.7,
    "end": 83.52,
    "text": "And then they'll leap to an unsupported or unjustified conclusion that has no evidence"
   },
   {
    "id": "t41",
    "start": 83.52,
    "end": 87.36,
    "text": "supporting it and an abundance of evidence counteracting it, like that fruit is making"
   },
   {
    "id": "t42",
    "start": 87.36,
    "end": 91.2,
    "text": "Americans fat. We do not have an issue with Americans eating too much fruit. In"
   },
   {
    "id": "t43",
    "start": 91.2,
    "end": 95.64,
    "text": "fact, nearly 90% of Americans don't even meat recommended and take a fruit. We"
   },
   {
    "id": "t44",
    "start": 95.64,
    "end": 99.16,
    "text": "have an issue consuming too much added sugar in general and too many nutrient"
   },
   {
    "id": "t45",
    "start": 99.16,
    "end": 102.6,
    "text": "poor calories for our needs. And where we really have an issue is podcasters"
   },
   {
    "id": "t46",
    "start": 102.6,
    "end": 105.64,
    "text": "with honor and confidence who are cosplaying as nutrition experts,"
   },
   {
    "id": "t47",
    "start": 105.64,
    "end": 111.36,
